    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as the premier play with an elite score of 73.32. He benefits from a favorable matchup against Michael McGreevy (xERA 4.39) and a significant park factor boost, making him our highest-projected asset for both power and potential counting stats. Following him, both **Brendan Donovan** (61.16) and **Will Smith** (61.79) anchor the core, with **Brendan Donovan** capitalizing on a massive 14% platoon edge against Mike Burrows, while **Will Smith** continues to provide high-floor production from the two-hole. **Masyn Winn** (60.60) also earns a strong recommendation, as the combination of an advantageous park and a manageable matchup against Jacob Lopez positions him as a high-value play despite his lower spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Drew Gilbert**, who fell just short of the 40-point threshold at 37.35. While the matchup against Emmet Sheehan isn't ideal, his exclusion was primarily driven by his projected spot at the bottom of the order and a lack of recent momentum relative to the starters. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee** against Sheehan; while their scores are respectable, the matchup against an elite arm (xERA 3.16) presents a significant ceiling risk. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Bryson Stott**, whose score of 45.09 is suppressed by his negative platoon split against Ranger Suarez and the threat of Suarez\u2019s ability to control the base paths\u2014an area where we prioritize speed efficiency. With **Yainer Diaz** still sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on **Cal Raleigh** to stabilize our catching production, even as he faces a slightly tougher environment today.",
